  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{X}-\\mathrm{X}-\\mathrm{X}-\\mathrm{X}-\\mathrm{X}$. The four digits 3, 3, 5,5 can be arranged at $(-)$ places in $\\frac{4 !}{2 ! 2 !}=6$ ways. The five digits $2,2,8,8,8$ can be arranged at $(X)$ places in $\\frac{5 !}{2 ! 3 !}$ ways $=10$ ways<br />Total no. of arrangements $=6 \\times 10=60$ ways",
